# CROSS-FILE IDENTIFIER BINDING FOR THE CANDIDATE BUNDLES (WFInputs section 3).
#
# The eleven case-local candidate bundles carry {policy,abi,contracts,
# release-table,expected-report}.json bound by sha256 into artifact.json.
# c/check_harness.py validates each sidecar in isolation. It does NOT check
# that an identifier written in one sidecar resolves in another, so a policy
# could bind a release id that no release table declares, name an audience
# principal that no policy declares, or replace the one fixed observation
# model, and every existing candidate-bundle test would still pass.
#
# tools/check_wfinputs.py implements the resolvable-reference fragment of
# WFInputs(M,ABI,R,K,TE,FPT,I,T) that is expressible against these mirrors:
#   item 3   dom(M.releaseBindings) = dom(R), and every audience, footprint,
#            carrier, component, root, placement and bound reference resolves
#   items 3/4 release footprints resolve to declared policy components
#   items 3/7 every release carrier has one declared mechanism contract
#   items 1/2/10 every visibility basis is total in the declared principals
#   item 11  the timing environment completely types the timing model
#   section 7 the single fixed observation model Theta_ct
#   section 2.5.1 the REQUIRED explicit empty TimingEnvironmentContract
#
# WHAT A GREEN RUN HERE DOES NOT MEAN. This is tier CandidateOnly. It does not
# establish WFInputs (items 4, 5, 9, 10, 12 and 14 quantify over the frozen
# reparsed module and a satisfiability obligation that do not exist here), does
# not establish NFConforms, and computes no ModelStatus, DeploymentStatus,
# PolicyReviewStatus, receipt, or witness. The local toolchain is LLVM 17.0.6;
# the normative boundary is 22.1.8 and is absent. Silence proves nothing.
#
# The negative arms follow integration/candidate-bundles/interfaces-negative.test: copy the tree
# into a per-arm isolated root, mutate exactly one field, REPAIR
# the artifact.json sidecar digest so the envelope binding is not what fails,
# and assert the specific diagnostic. Each arm gets its own root so one
# mutation cannot mask or be masked by another.

# --- positive arm: the real tree binds ---------------------------------------
# RUN: %python %harness/tools/check_wfinputs.py 2>&1 | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CLEAN
# CLEAN: wfinputs binding checks passed: 11 candidate bundles
# CLEAN: checked: cross-file identifier resolution
# CLEAN: not checked: WFInputs items 4, 5, 9, 10, 12, 14

# Non-vacuity for the timing migration: the explicit empty contract is present
# in ALL ELEVEN bundles, not merely somewhere. Pinned as a count, because
# presence is the easy half.
# RUN: grep -l '"latencyClassId": "lat.fixed.1"' %fixtures/*/*/candidate/contracts.json | wc -l | tr -d ' ' | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=TIMINGCOUNT
# TIMINGCOUNT: {{^11$}}
# And every one of them is the EMPTY contract: an empty choice domain,
# occurrence map, latency table and coupling map (spec section 2.5.1). Four
# empty fields across eleven bundles is exactly 44 lines; a bundle that dropped
# or populated any one of them moves the count.
# RUN: grep -hE '"(choiceDomain|latencyMeaning)": \[\]|"(occurrences|pairedChoiceCoupling)": \{\}' %fixtures/*/*/candidate/contracts.json | wc -l | tr -d ' ' | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=EMPTYTE
# EMPTYTE: {{^44$}}

# The retired audience bundle was the only Candidate-v2 release-table instance.
# Its replacement uses authoring contracts for cross-host transfers, which the
# Candidate-v2 mirrors cannot express. The old release-domain negative arms are
# therefore removed rather than kept alive with fabricated release semantics.

# --- shared tree setup for the remaining negative arms -----------------------
# RUN: rm -rf %t.d %t.e

# --- (d) the fixed observation model is replaced -----------------------------
# Spec section 7 fixes exactly one observation model for Rev-4 and states that
# removing or coarsening an event kind or field is not configuration. There is
# no second legal value for this field, so a swapped name is not a variant
# profile, it is an unmodelled one. No reason class is quoted here, because the
# corpus does not state which PublicReasonClassesV2 member applies.
# RUN: mkdir -p %t.d/tools
# RUN: cp %harness/tools/check_wfinputs.py %t.d/tools/check_wfinputs.py
# RUN: cp %harness/tools/fixture_layout.py %t.d/tools/fixture_layout.py
# RUN: cp %harness/tools/checkpoint_model.py %t.d/tools/checkpoint_model.py
# RUN: cp -R %fixtures %t.d/fixtures
# RUN: %python -c "import hashlib,json,pathlib; root=pathlib.Path(r'%t.d/fixtures/abi-alias/disjoint-control/candidate'); side=root/'policy.json'; value=json.loads(side.read_text()); value['fixed_observation_model']='Theta_something_else_entirely'; side.write_text(json.dumps(value,indent=2)+'\n'); identity_path=root/'artifact.json'; identity=json.loads(identity_path.read_text()); identity['candidate_sidecar_sha256']['policy.json']=hashlib.sha256(side.read_bytes()).hexdigest(); identity_path.write_text(json.dumps(identity,indent=2)+'\n')"
# RUN: not %python %t.d/tools/check_wfinputs.py 2>&1 | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=THETA
# THETA: fixtures/abi-alias/disjoint-control/candidate/policy.json: fixed_observation_model: 'Theta_something_else_entirely' is not the single Rev-4 observation model 'Theta_ct'; coarsening or replacing an event kind is not configuration (spec section 7 and WFInputs item 1)
# THETA: wfinputs binding checks failed

# --- (e) the explicit empty TimingEnvironmentContract is deleted -------------
# Spec section 2.5.1 makes the explicit empty contract REQUIRED when no ideal
# timing choice is modelled. Deleting it leaves "timing_contracts": [] behind,
# which is exactly the pre-migration state of these bundles: the ABSENCE of the
# required object rather than an instance of it. The tool must not accept the
# absence as an empty model.
# RUN: mkdir -p %t.e/tools
# RUN: cp %harness/tools/check_wfinputs.py %t.e/tools/check_wfinputs.py
# RUN: cp %harness/tools/fixture_layout.py %t.e/tools/fixture_layout.py
# RUN: cp %harness/tools/checkpoint_model.py %t.e/tools/checkpoint_model.py
# RUN: cp -R %fixtures %t.e/fixtures
# RUN: %python -c "import hashlib,json,pathlib; root=pathlib.Path(r'%t.e/fixtures/launder-scan/model-clean-p4-open/candidate'); side=root/'contracts.json'; value=json.loads(side.read_text()); del value['timing_environment']; side.write_text(json.dumps(value,indent=2)+'\n'); identity_path=root/'artifact.json'; identity=json.loads(identity_path.read_text()); identity['candidate_sidecar_sha256']['contracts.json']=hashlib.sha256(side.read_bytes()).hexdigest(); identity_path.write_text(json.dumps(identity,indent=2)+'\n')"
# RUN: not %python %t.e/tools/check_wfinputs.py 2>&1 | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NOTIMING
# NOTIMING: fixtures/launder-scan/model-clean-p4-open/candidate/contracts.json: timing_environment: the explicit empty TimingEnvironmentContract is absent; an empty timing_contracts array is the absence of the required object, not an instance of it (spec section 2.5.1 and WFInputs item 11)
# NOTIMING: wfinputs binding checks failed
# The surviving empty timing_contracts array is still there and did not rescue it.
# RUN: grep -c '"timing_contracts": \[\]' %t.e/fixtures/launder-scan/model-clean-p4-open/candidate/contracts.json | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=STALETC
# STALETC: {{^1$}}
